  "result": "`satisfies(version, range)` is now implemented in `src/semver.js` following `docs/SPEC.md`, and `npm test` passes (12 of 12). The new tests are in `test/satisfies.test.js`.\n\nThe tests cover each section of the spec: version parsing, ordering, `||` and AND, x-ranges, tilde, caret, hyphen ranges, and the prerelease rule. They also check that invalid versions or ranges return `false` without throwing.\n\nThe spec doesn't settle a few cases, so I chose:\n- `>*` and `<*` match nothing, while `>=*` and `<=*` match any non-prerelease version.\n- Numeric prerelease identifiers may have leading zeros, because the spec only forbids them in `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`.\n- A prerelease on a partial version (such as `1.2-beta`) is invalid.",
